### SC3: Timeout and Abort Architecture (G-05)

**Target state:**
A client-side hook or utility at
`app/components/features/basket/checkout/useCheckoutAction.ts` that
owns the AbortController, the 10-second timeout, and dispatches
FAIL_NETWORK or PASS_VALIDATION/FAIL_VALIDATION to the machine.
Exactly matches §6 implementation pattern.

**Files owned by this contract:**
  - app/components/features/basket/checkout/useCheckoutAction.ts (CREATE)

**DoD (Sequenced):**

✔ [ ] Pass 1 — Skeleton: @done(26-04-06 15:57)
      Create useCheckoutAction.ts:
        "use client"
        export function useCheckoutAction(
          dispatch: (event: PreCheckoutEvent) => void
        ): { executeValidation: (payload: BasketPayload, idempotencyKey: string) => void }
      Body: stub returning no-op.
      /test: `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.

✔ [ ] Pass 2 — AbortController + timeout wiring: @done(26-04-06 16:02)
      Implement per §6 exactly:
        const controller = new AbortController();
        const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 10_000);
        try {
          const result = await validateBasket(payload, idempotencyKey,
                                              { signal: controller.signal });
          clearTimeout(timeoutId);
          if (result.outcome === "PASS") {
            dispatch({ type: "PASS_VALIDATION", stripeUrl: result.stripeUrl });
          } else if (result.outcome === "FAIL_VALIDATION") {
            dispatch({ type: "FAIL_VALIDATION", payload: result.discrepancy });
          } else {
            dispatch({ type: "FAIL_NETWORK" });
          }
        } catch (error) {
          clearTimeout(timeoutId);
          dispatch({ type: "FAIL_NETWORK" });
        }
      The AbortController is created inside executeValidation (call-site scoped),
      NOT in useState or useRef. This ensures unmount does not suppress FAIL_NETWORK.
      /test: unit tests in tests/unit/preCheckout/useCheckoutAction.test.ts:
              - Mock validateBasket returning PASS → PASS_VALIDATION dispatched
              - Mock validateBasket returning FAIL_VALIDATION → FAIL_VALIDATION dispatched
              - Mock validateBasket returning FAIL_NETWORK → FAIL_NETWORK dispatched
              - Mock validateBasket throwing AbortError → FAIL_NETWORK dispatched
              - Mock validateBasket throwing generic Error → FAIL_NETWORK dispatched
              - Timer fires after 10000ms mock: abort() called on controller
            Run: `npx vitest run tests/unit/preCheckout/`

✔ [ ] Neighbour flow sync check: @done(26-04-06 16:25)
      Verify: dispatch function signature matches PreCheckoutEvent union from SC1.
      Verify: BasketPayload consumed here matches shape produced by basketStore.
      ✔ Write integration test @done(26-04-06 16:25)

✔ [ ] Global flow sync check: @done(26-04-06 16:28)
      Verify: No direct Stripe SDK import in this file — all Stripe work is
              server-side in SC2.
      Verify: validateBasket import path resolves through the "use server" boundary
              correctly (Next.js App Router server action import rules).
      ✔ write test @done(26-04-06 16:28)

