### SC5: Accept & Continue Guard and Basket Mutation (G-08)

**Target state:**
A mutation handler at
`app/components/features/basket/checkout/useAcceptDiscrepancies.ts`
that applies basket store mutations for each discrepancy type before
dispatching START_VALIDATION. Implements the §7 guard condition as code,
not as a UI convention.

**Files owned by this contract:**
  - app/components/features/basket/checkout/useAcceptDiscrepancies.ts (CREATE)

**DoD (Sequenced):**

- [ ] Pass 1 — Skeleton:
      Create useAcceptDiscrepancies.ts:
        "use client"
        export function useAcceptDiscrepancies(
          dispatch: (event: PreCheckoutEvent) => void,
          executeValidation: ReturnType<typeof useCheckoutAction>["executeValidation"],
          basketPayload: BasketPayload
        ): {
          acceptAndContinue: (discrepancy: DiscrepancyPayload,
                              idempotencyKey: string) => Promise<void>;
        }
      Body: stub.
      /test: `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.

- [ ] Pass 2 — Mutation logic per §7:
      Implement acceptAndContinue:
        if (discrepancy.type === "STRIPE_CONFIG") {
          // No mutation possible. Do not dispatch START_VALIDATION.
          // Log warning. Button should have been hidden — this is a safety guard.
          return;
        }
        let mutationsSucceeded = true;
        try {
          if (discrepancy.type === "PRICE") {
            for (const item of discrepancy.items) {
              basketStore.updateItemPrice(item.id, item.actual);
              // If basketStore throws: mutationsSucceeded = false; break;
            }
          }
          if (discrepancy.type === "INVENTORY") {
            for (const item of discrepancy.items) {
              if (item.available === 0) {
                basketStore.removeItem(item.id);
              } else {
                basketStore.updateItemQuantity(item.id, item.available);
              }
            }
          }
        } catch {
          mutationsSucceeded = false;
        }
        if (!mutationsSucceeded) {
          // Do not dispatch START_VALIDATION. Surface error to user (separate concern).
          return;
        }
        // Mutations succeeded. Now dispatch (new idempotency key generated inside machine).
        const newKey = crypto.randomUUID();
        dispatch({ type: "START_VALIDATION" });
        executeValidation(basketPayload, newKey);
      /test: unit tests in tests/unit/preCheckout/useAcceptDiscrepancies.test.ts:
              - PRICE discrepancy: basketStore.updateItemPrice called for each item
                with item.actual; START_VALIDATION dispatched; executeValidation called
              - INVENTORY discrepancy available > 0: updateItemQuantity called
              - INVENTORY discrepancy available === 0: removeItem called
              - STRIPE_CONFIG: no dispatch, no executeValidation call
              - Mutation throws: no dispatch, no executeValidation call
            Run: `npx vitest run tests/unit/preCheckout/useAcceptDiscrepancies.test.ts`

- [ ] Neighbour flow sync check:
      Verify: basketStore.updateItemPrice, updateItemQuantity, removeItem API matches
              actual basketStore exports. Read basketStore.ts before implementing.
              Do not assume method names — read source of truth.
      Verify: After mutations, basketStore state is consistent with what the next
              validateBasket call will receive. Do a manual trace: mutated basket →
              SC2 Step 1 Sanity fetch → should pass if mutations were correct.

- [ ] Global flow sync check:
      Verify: Basket mutations here do not corrupt the basket for the downstream
              order creation step. The downstream order is built from the same
              basket store; mutated prices/quantities must be intentional and
              clearly documented for the downstream chunk.

**Delegation:**
  Execute: `/implement SC5 — Accept & Continue guard and basket mutation`
  Build:   `/build useAcceptDiscrepancies Pass1 Skeleton`
           `/build useAcceptDiscrepancies Pass2 MutationLogic`
  Verify:  `/test tests/unit/preCheckout/useAcceptDiscrepancies.test.ts`

