### SC7: Cancel URL Back-Navigation Handler (G-10)

**Target state:**
The basket page component detects `?checkout=cancelled` query param on mount,
dispatches RESET if machine is in SUCCESS state, and cleans the URL.
Per §9 "Cancel URL and back-navigation".

**Files owned by this contract:**
  - app/components/features/basket/BasketPage.tsx  (EDIT — add handler only)

**DoD (Sequenced):**

- [ ] Pass 1 — Skeleton:
      In BasketPage.tsx, add a useEffect that reads searchParams for
      `checkout=cancelled`. Body: no-op. Confirm it does not break existing render.
      /test: `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.

- [ ] Pass 2 — Handler logic:
      Implement per §9:
        useEffect(() => {
          const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
          if (params.get("checkout") === "cancelled") {
            if (checkoutState === "SUCCESS") {
              reset(); // dispatches RESET from SUCCESS → fires lock release
            }
            // Clean URL regardless of state to prevent re-trigger on re-render
            const cleanUrl = window.location.pathname;
            window.history.replaceState({}, "", cleanUrl);
          }
        }, []);  // Runs once on mount only
      /test: unit test (jsdom):
              - URL has ?checkout=cancelled AND state is SUCCESS:
                reset() called; URL cleaned
              - URL has ?checkout=cancelled AND state is ERROR_NETWORK:
                reset() called (harmless); URL cleaned
              - URL has ?checkout=cancelled AND state is IDLE:
                URL cleaned; no dispatch
              - URL does NOT have param: no effect
            Run: `npx vitest run tests/unit/preCheckout/basketCancelHandler.test.tsx`

- [ ] Pass 3 — Desktop layout (1280px):
      No visual change — URL param handling has no UI output.

- [ ] Neighbour flow sync check:
      Verify: The cancel_url set in SC2 validateBasket exactly matches the
              basket page route + `?checkout=cancelled` param.
      Verify: The success_url set in SC2 does NOT route back to basket page
              (would trigger cancel handler erroneously).

- [ ] Global flow sync check:
      Verify: If Stripe posts back to cancel_url with additional Stripe params
              (e.g. session_id), the handler does not break. It only checks
              `checkout=cancelled`; other params are ignored.

**Delegation:**
  Execute: `/implement SC7 — Cancel URL handler in BasketPage`
  Build:   `/build BasketPage Pass1 CancelHandlerSkeleton`
           `/build BasketPage Pass2 CancelHandlerLogic`
  Verify:  `/test tests/unit/preCheckout/basketCancelHandler.test.tsx`

