## PHASE 6: POST-SPRINT /LEARN (MANDATORY)

After sprint lock, execute `/learn` protocol:

  Lessons to codify:
    1. "AbortController must be call-site scoped, not stored in useState or useRef,
       to ensure timeout fires on component unmount."
       Severity: Critical. Tag: abort-controller, checkout, state-machine.

    2. "Never call redirect() inside a server action that is called from a client
       component — return the URL and navigate client-side with window.location.assign()."
       Severity: Critical. Tag: next-redirect, server-action, stripe.

    3. "Idempotency key must be UUIDv4 per-attempt, not basket ID. Basket ID causes
       15-minute cache collision on retry after basket mutation."
       Severity: Critical. Tag: idempotency, stripe, checkout.

    4. "RESET from SUCCESS must be fire-and-forget for lock release. Never block
       the state transition on async I/O."
       Severity: High. Tag: inventory-lock, state-machine, inngest.

    5. "Stripe 400 is FAIL_VALIDATION not FAIL_NETWORK. Retrying a 400 with the
       same params produces the same 400. Always generate a new idempotency key
       after any failure."
       Severity: High. Tag: stripe, error-handling, idempotency.

  Update _project/lessons/INDEX.md with above entries.
  Update .windsurfrules if any lesson qualifies as a universal constraint.

