## SPRINT LOCK CRITERIA

The sprint is locked ONLY when ALL of the following pass:

  [ ] npx tsc --noEmit — zero errors across entire project
  [ ] npx vitest run tests/unit/preCheckout/ — 100% pass
  [ ] npx vitest run tests/integration/checkout/ — 100% pass
  [ ] npx playwright test tests/e2e/checkout/basket_to_checkout/ — 100% pass
  [ ] npx next build — zero warnings about server-only boundary violations
  [ ] Manual state machine invariant checklist:
      [ ] IDLE → START_VALIDATION → PROCESSING (10s timer active)
      [ ] PROCESSING → PASS_VALIDATION → SUCCESS → window.location.assign fired
      [ ] SUCCESS → 5s elapses → ERROR_NETWORK (watchdog)
      [ ] SUCCESS → RESET → IDLE (lock release fire-and-forget confirmed in network tab)
      [ ] PROCESSING → FAIL_NETWORK (abort after 10s) → ERROR_NETWORK
      [ ] ERROR_NETWORK → START_VALIDATION (Retry) → PROCESSING (fresh key confirmed in request header)
      [ ] PROCESSING → FAIL_VALIDATION PRICE → ERROR_VALIDATION (prices shown in UI)
      [ ] ERROR_VALIDATION → acceptAndContinue (PRICE) → basket updated → PROCESSING (fresh key)
      [ ] PROCESSING → FAIL_VALIDATION INVENTORY → ERROR_VALIDATION (stock shown)
      [ ] ERROR_VALIDATION → acceptAndContinue (INVENTORY) → basket updated → PROCESSING
      [ ] ERROR_VALIDATION STRIPE_CONFIG → no "Accept & Continue" button visible
      [ ] ERROR_VALIDATION → RESET → IDLE (basket editable again)
      [ ] Navigate to basket page with ?checkout=cancelled + machine in SUCCESS → RESET fired, lock released, URL cleaned
  [ ] Regression: baseline test counts match or improve (zero new failures)
  [ ] Proof of Wholeness: this chunk delivers a complete IDLE → SUCCESS redirect path
      with all failure branches handled, all invariants enforced, and no inventory
      lock can be left orphaned by any client-side event including component unmount,
      redirect failure, or back navigation from Stripe.

